& [BoundaryImportMap: FSC2BoundaryAndInvariantMapV1] is the imported boundary map for FSC2 planning coordination
  + [slice_id] is FSC2-S01
  + [source_chunk] is FSC1 foundation contracts
  + [target_chunk] is FSC2 planning coordination
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_boundary_input_sha256] is 5DEA75196054BAC4C3DFD2B1EAEEFC4C28316CEE7E5191B60C7F32CA4F03DEA8
  + [import_policy] is read_only_import
  + [refinement_policy] is FSC2 may define new planning-coordination contracts that consume imported records and operators without mutating FSC1 outputs
  + [implementation_policy] is no runtime implementation is authorized by this map alone

  = must: treat imported FSC1 outputs as accepted boundary inputs, not editable local drafts
  = must: keep readiness, packetization, coordination, and completion-delta dependencies inside FSC2
  = must: route meaning, authority, ambiguity, stale support, and conflict resolution back through SOP-first review
  - never: let projection surfaces, chat logs, runtime graphs, or generated SQLite rows outrank SOP authority records

& [ImportedRecordKindInventory] is the FSC1 record inventory imported into FSC2
  + [record_kind] is source_log
  + [record_kind] is log_entry
  + [record_kind] is citation_ref
  + [record_kind] is narrative_node
  + [record_kind] is understanding_anchor
  + [record_kind] is capability_node
  + [record_kind] is requirement_record
  + [record_kind] is support_record
  + [record_kind] is support_gap
  + [record_kind] is authority_artifact
  + [record_kind] is coordination_claim
  + [record_kind] is operator_contract
  + [record_kind] is operator_trace
  + [record_kind] is work_packet
  + [record_kind] is completion_review
  + [record_kind] is readiness_projection
  + [record_kind] is stale_projection
  + [record_kind] is proof_result
  + [record_kind] is fault_record
  + [record_kind_count] is 19

  = must: preserve imported common fields record_id, record_kind, natural_key, subject_ref, authority_state, source_ref_set, lineage_edge_set, freshness_rule, and status
  = must: preserve source/projection distinctions when FSC2 creates derived readiness, packet, claim, trace, review, proof, stale, or fault records
  = must: use imported natural-key and lifecycle rules unless an FSC2 completion review explicitly routes a rebake request upstream

& [ImportedOperatorAndStorageInventory] is the FSC1 operator and storage inventory imported into FSC2
  + [operator_template] is OperatorContractTemplateV1
  + [foundation_operator_contract] is signature_validation
  + [foundation_operator_contract] is support_readiness_recompute
  + [foundation_operator_contract] is work_packet_generation v1_stub
  + [storage_pattern] is hybrid SOP authority files plus rebuildable SQLite derived index
  + [fixture_basis] is FoundationFixturePlanV1
  + [fixture_basis] is FoundationFixtureIndexV1

  = must: use OperatorContractTemplateV1 for FSC2 operator contracts
  = must: treat support_readiness_recompute as the foundation readiness contract that FSC2 refines for planning coordination
  = must: refine work_packet_generation beyond v1_stub inside FSC2 before a packet can be treated as accepted work authority
  = must: keep SQLite rebuildable from SOP authority and operator traces

& [FSC2OwnedInvariantSet] is the invariant set owned by FSC2
  + [invariant] is imported FSC1 outputs are read-only boundary inputs
  + [invariant] is readiness projection never creates work packets by itself
  + [invariant] is work packets require accepted readiness, dependency closure, support_delta obligations, requirement_delta obligations, and coordination prerequisites
  + [invariant] is coordination claims coordinate ownership and conflict signals but do not override source specification authority
  + [invariant] is completion reviews must classify support_delta and requirement_delta before opening the next work slice
  + [invariant] is blocked, stale, contradicted, ambiguous, and faulted states cannot produce ready work packets
  + [invariant] is generated indexes, chat surfaces, runtime checkpoints, and adapters are projections unless separately promoted through SOP authority
  + [invariant] is every FSC2 operator must emit operator_trace, proof_result, stale_projection, support_gap, or fault_record as appropriate when it refuses mutation

  = must: preserve these invariants through FSC2-S02 through FSC2-S07
  = must: mark downstream FSC2 slices stale when any invariant changes

& [ForbiddenMutationList: FSC2] is the forbidden mutation set for FSC2-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC1 output files to make FSC2 easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is changing imported record schemas or natural-key lifecycle rules
  + [forbidden_mutation] is changing foundation operator semantics in place
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating work_packet_generation v1_stub as production packetization
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing LangGraph runtime nodes
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing IRC, Matrix, web, Codex, terminal, or Langflow adapters
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing mailbox transport
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching real work from an unaccepted packet
  + [forbidden_mutation] is granting operations-manager authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating generated SQLite files as source authority

  = must: fail FSC2-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: FSC2] is the stale trigger set for FSC2 downstream work
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC1 foundation contract pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC2 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is imported record schema or natural-key matrix changes
  + [stale_trigger] is imported operator template or foundation operator contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is storage decision changes source/projection authority
  + [stale_trigger] is readiness contract changes after packet contract work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is packet contract changes after coordination contract work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is coordination claim contract changes after completion-review gate work starts
  + [stale_trigger] is completion-review gate changes after fixture planning starts
  + [stale_trigger] is unresolved support_delta or requirement_delta appears in completed work review
  + [stale_trigger] is false-ready work packet, false-ready next gate, or unresolved coordination conflict is detected

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review rather than silent edits

& [FSC2S01AcceptanceChecklist] is the verification checklist for FSC2-S01
  + [required_component] is imported record-kind inventory
  + [required_component] is imported operator contract inventory
  + [required_component] is storage and fixture import inventory
  + [required_component] is FSC2-owned invariant set
  + [required_component] is forbidden mutation list
  + [required_component] is downstream stale trigger list
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is FSC1 source edit
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is readiness operator finalization
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is packetization operator finalization
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is coordination claim finalization
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is runtime implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations control

  = must: accept FSC2-S01 only when the boundary imports are mapped without mutating their authority
